## What Happened

In .NET 11, **DSA (Digital Signature Algorithm) was removed from macOS**. Calling `DSA.Create()` now throws at runtime on macOS. Windows and Linux are unaffected.

## How to Fix

Since you only need to **verify** legacy signatures (not generate new ones), you have two options:

### Option 1: Use a platform guard (keeps macOS builds working)

```csharp
if (OperatingSystem.IsMacOS())
    throw new PlatformNotSupportedException("DSA verification not supported on macOS in .NET 11");

using var dsa = DSA.Create();
dsa.ImportParameters(legacyPublicKey);
bool valid = dsa.VerifyData(data, signature, HashAlgorithmName.SHA1);
```

### Option 2 (recommended): Migrate away from DSA entirely

Re-sign your artifacts with a modern algorithm and verify with **ECDsa** or **RSA**:

```csharp
using var ecdsa = ECDsa.Create();
ecdsa.ImportSubjectPublicKeyInfo(publicKeyBytes, out _);
bool valid = ecdsa.VerifyData(data, signature, HashAlgorithmName.SHA256);
```

### If you must verify legacy DSA signatures on macOS

Run the verification on a Linux or Windows service/container, since DSA still works there. There is no workaround to make DSA function on macOS with .NET 11.
